# ABP Framework

ABP is a complete application framework for building modern web applications following best practices and conventions.

## Key Features
- **Modularity**: Compose applications from reusable modules
- **DDD Support**: Domain-driven design patterns out of the box
- **Multi-Tenancy**: First-class SaaS support
- **Authorization**: Permission-based authorization
- **Auto API**: Application services become REST APIs automatically

## Solution Layers
```
*.Domain.Shared    → Constants, enums, DTOs shared with clients
*.Domain           → Entities, domain services, repository interfaces
*.Application.Contracts → App service interfaces, input/output DTOs
*.Application      → App service implementations
*.EntityFrameworkCore → EF Core DbContext, repositories
*.HttpApi          → REST API controllers
*.Web              → UI (MVC/Blazor/Angular)
```

## Quick Patterns

### Entity
```csharp
public class Book : AggregateRoot<Guid>
{
    public string Name { get; private set; }
    protected Book() { }
    public Book(Guid id, string name) : base(id) { Name = name; }
}
```

### Application Service
```csharp
public class BookAppService : ApplicationService, IBookAppService
{
    public async Task<BookDto> GetAsync(Guid id)
    {
        var book = await _repository.GetAsync(id);
        return ObjectMapper.Map<Book, BookDto>(book);
    }
}
```

### Permission
```csharp
[Authorize(BookStorePermissions.Books.Create)]
public async Task<BookDto> CreateAsync(CreateBookDto input) { }
```
